  "content": {
    "id": "p51-q28-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "28",
    "prompt": "Molly has a bottle of 15% strength cordial and wants to make it stronger.\nShe adds an amount of 100% strength cordial to her bottle to make a total of 2000 mL of drink.\nIf the final strength of the drink is 25% cordial, find the amount of 100% strength cordial added.\nRound your answer to the nearest mL.\n\nLet $y$ be the volume (in mL) of initial 15% strength cordial.\nLet $x$ be the volume (in mL) of 100% strength cordial that Molly adds.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$235\\text{ mL}$",
      "worked": "Using the given variables,\n$$\\begin{align*}x+y&=2000 &&(1)\\\\x+0.15y&=0.25(2000)\\\\x+0.15y&=500 &&(2)\\end{align*}$$\n$(2)-0.15\\times(1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x+0.15y-0.15(x+y)&=500-0.15(2000)\\\\0.85x&=200\\\\x&=\\frac{4000}{17}\\\\x&\\approx235\\text{ mL}\\end{align*}$$\nMolly adds 235 mL of 100% strength cordial, to the nearest mL.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
